   "len": 90,
   "first": 6634,
   "line": "Meanwhile, out west, skies were clear.",
   "note": "ch5"
  },
  {
   "id": "S87",
   "size": "wide",
   "key": 73,
   "len": 118,
   "first": 6724,
   "line": "In Texas, one person saw them fall like a gigantic umbrella.",
   "note": "ch5"
  },
  {
   "id": "S88",
   "size": "tilt",
   "key": 46,
   "len": 75,
   "first": 6842,
   "line": "Right out of the head of Leo, the Lion.",
   "note": "ch5"
  },
  {
   "id": "S89",
   "size": "insert",
   "key": 53,
   "len": 86,
   "first": 6917,
   "line": "You, with a real umbrella, would still get wet.",
   "note": "ch5"
  },
  {
   "id": "S90",
   "size": "med",
   "key": 45,
   "len": 72,
   "first": 7003,
   "line": "So you'd better pray for clear skies.",
   "note": "ch5"
  },
  {
   "id": "S91",
   "size": "high",
   "key": 62,
   "len": 100,
   "first": 7075,
   "line": "Because the whole show depends on one thing.",
   "note": "ch5"
  },
  {
   "id": "S92",
   "size": "med",
   "key": 42,
   "len": 67,
   "first": 7175,
   "line": "So, here is the catch for this year.",
   "note": "ch6"
  },
  {
   "id": "S93",
   "size": "wide",
   "key": 52,
   "len": 84,
   "first": 7242,
   "line": "Right now, Tempel-Tuttle is past Saturn.",
   "note": "ch6"
  },
  {
   "id": "S94",
   "size": "pullout",
   "key": 76,
   "len": 123,
   "first": 7326,
   "line": "About one billion seven hundred ninety million kilometres from the Sun.",
   "note": "ch6"
  },
  {
   "id": "S95",
   "size": "pan",
   "key": 51,
   "len": 82,
   "first": 7449,
   "line": "It is slowly crawling back toward the Sun.",
   "note": "ch6"
  },
  {
   "id": "S96",
   "size": "high",
   "key": 52,
   "len": 84,
   "first": 7531,
   "line": "But the part of the trail Earth crosses this week?",
   "note": "ch6"
  },
  {
   "id": "S97",
   "size": "low",
   "key": 22,
   "len": 36,
   "first": 7615,
   "line": "Almost empty.",
   "note": "ch6"
  },
  {
   "id": "S98",
   "size": "close",
   "key": 74,
   "len": 119,
   "first": 7651,
   "line": "Just a few scattered crumbs, loose for a thousand years or two.",
   "note": "ch6"
  },
  {
   "id": "S99",
   "size": "wide",
   "key": 43,
   "len": 69,
   "first": 7770,
   "line": "So no storm. Not this week.",
   "note": "ch6"
  },
  {
   "id": "S100",
   "size": "med",
   "key": 59,
   "len": 95,
   "first": 7839,
   "line": "Experts expect long stretches of nothing at all.",
   "note": "ch6"
  },
  {
   "id": "S101",
   "size": "pullout",
   "key": 60,
   "len": 96,
   "first": 7934,
   "line": "Which makes the next question the real one.",
   "note": "ch6"
  },
  {
   "id": "S102",
   "size": "wide",
   "key": 35,
   "len": 57,
   "first": 8030,
   "line": "So what will you actually see?",
   "note": "ch7"
  },
  {
   "id": "S103",
   "size": "high",
   "key": 64,
   "len": 104,
   "first": 8087,
   "line": "The Leonids peak on the seventeenth and eighteenth of November.",
   "note": "ch7"
  },
  {
   "id": "S104",
   "size": "med",
   "key": 83,
   "len": 134,
   "first": 8191,
   "line": "The IMO puts the peak at quarter to midnight UTC, the seventeenth.",
   "note": "ch7"
  },
  {
   "id": "S105",
   "size": "pan",
   "key": 69,
   "len": 111,
   "first": 8325,
   "line": "NASA says: look before dawn, after the Moon sets.",
   "note": "ch7"
  },
  {
   "id": "S106",
   "size": "tilt",
   "key": 43,
   "len": 69,
   "first": 8436,
   "line": "Leo climbs higher after midnight.",
   "note": "ch7"
  },
  {
   "id": "S107",
   "size": "close",
   "key": 50,
   "len": 81,
   "first": 8505,
   "line": "Up to fifteen an hour, if everything goes right.",
   "note": "ch7"
  },
  {
   "id": "S108",
   "size": "low",
   "key": 34,
   "len": 55,
   "first": 8586,
   "line": "Most people will see fewer.",
   "note": "ch7"
  },
  {
   "id": "S109",
   "size": "wide",
   "key": 32,
   "len": 52,
   "first": 8641,
   "line": "But look at who is next to them.",
   "note": "ch7"
  },
  {
   "id": "S110",
   "size": "pan",
   "key": 76,
   "len": 123,
   "first": 8693,
   "line": "On the fifteenth and sixteenth, Mars and Jupiter sit side by side.",
   "note": "ch7"
  },
  {
   "id": "S111",
   "size": "insert",
   "key": 40,
   "len": 65,
   "first": 8816,
   "line": "Only one point two degrees apart.",
   "note": "ch7"
  },
  {
   "id": "S112",
   "size": "med",
   "key": 40,
   "len": 64,
   "first": 8881,
   "line": "That is about two Moons wide.",
   "note": "ch7"
  },
  {
   "id": "S113",
   "size": "high",
   "key": 61,
   "len": 98,
   "first": 8945,
   "line": "Find a dark spot, and give your eyes half an hour.",
   "note": "ch7"
  },
  {
   "id": "S114",
   "size": "med",
   "key": 56,
   "len": 91,
   "first": 9043,
   "line": "Bring a blanket. A flask. A friend.",
   "note": "ch7"
  },
  {
   "id": "S115",
   "size": "pullout",
   "key": 46,
   "len": 74,
   "first": 9134,
   "line": "And look at as much of the sky as you can.",
   "note": "ch7"
  },
  {
   "id": "S116",
   "size": "close",
   "key": 79,
   "len": 127,
   "first": 9208,
   "line": "One streak is plenty. It is the fastest thing you will ever see.",
   "note": "ch7"
  },
  {
   "id": "S117",
   "size": "low",
   "key": 58,
   "len": 94,
   "first": 9335,
   "line": "Forty-five miles a second, remember.",
   "note": "ch7"
  },
  {
   "id": "S118",
   "size": "wide",
   "key": 42,
   "len": 67,
   "first": 9429,
   "line": "So when does the sky let go again?",
   "note": "ch8"
  },
  {
   "id": "S119",
   "size": "pan",
   "key": 31,
   "len": 50,
   "first": 9496,
   "line": "Not for a while, sadly.",
   "note": "ch8"
  },
  {
   "id": "S120",
   "size": "high",
   "key": 85,
   "len": 137,
   "first": 9546,
   "line": "In twenty twenty-nine, Jupiter is expected to nudge the comet off course.",
   "note": "ch8"
  },
  {
   "id": "S121",
   "size": "med",
   "key": 76,
   "len": 122,
   "first": 9683,
   "line": "After that, a repeat of the great storm is basically off the table.",
   "note": "ch8"
  },
  {
   "id": "S122",
   "size": "close",
   "key": 36,
   "len": 58,
   "first": 9805,
   "line": "Basically. Not quite.",
   "note": "ch8"
  },
  {
   "id": "S123",
   "size": "wide",
   "key": 78,
   "len": 125,
   "first": 9863,
   "line": "One French expert forecast a big burst in twenty thirty-four.",
   "note": "ch8"
  },
  {
   "id": "S124",
   "size": "low",
   "key": 32,
   "len": 51,
   "first": 9988,
   "line": "Up to two thousand an hour.",
   "note": "ch8"
  },
  {
   "id": "S125",
   "size": "med",
   "key": 29,
   "len": 46,
   "first": 10039,
   "line": "That is eight years from now.",
   "note": "ch8"
  },
  {
   "id": "S126",
   "size": "pan",
   "key": 66,
   "len": 107,
   "first": 10085,
   "line": "Not a storm like sixty-six, but a sky with hail in it.",
   "note": "ch8"
  },
  {
   "id": "S127",
   "size": "wide",
   "key": 44,
   "len": 71,
   "first": 10192,
   "line": "So, back to that mountain in Arizona.",
   "note": "ch8"
  },
  {
   "id": "S128",
   "size": "pullout",
   "key": 69,
   "len": 111,
   "first": 10263,
   "line": "Forty meteors a second, and you are the one standing under them.",
   "note": "ch8"
  },
  {
   "id": "S129",
   "size": "high",
   "key": 59,
   "len": 95,
   "first": 10374,
   "line": "You would never need to ask what the sky is made of again.",
   "note": "ch8"
  },
  {
   "id": "S130",
   "size": "close",
   "key": 29,
   "len": 47,
   "first": 10469,
   "line": "You would know it falls.",
   "note": "ch8"
  },
  {
   "id": "S131",
   "size": "med",
   "key": 74,
   "len": 120,
   "first": 10516,
   "line": "Which night would you pick: eighteen thirty-three, or sixty-six?",
   "note": "ch8"
  },
  {
   "id": "S132",
   "size": "wide",
   "key": 87,
   "len": 141,
   "first": 10636,
   "line": "Tomorrow: another what if, another piece of the sky.",
   "note": "ch8"
  }
 ],
